WEBVTT

00:07.730 --> 00:12.200
Les Misérables

00:07.730 --> 00:12.200
A Girl Named Cosette

00:08.740 --> 00:11.740
Beyond the wind

00:12.200 --> 00:15.620
Kaze ga fuki nuketeku

00:12.210 --> 00:15.600
The wind blows

00:15.630 --> 00:22.190
over the daisies blooming over the stone pavement

00:15.630 --> 00:22.190
Ishidatami ni saku hinagiku

00:22.220 --> 00:25.740
I held my knees

00:22.220 --> 00:25.740
Hiza wo tsuite

00:25.760 --> 00:31.200
and gazed at the flowers

00:25.760 --> 00:31.200
Jitto mitsumeteta

00:31.230 --> 00:34.960
Far away, very far away

00:31.230 --> 00:34.960
Tooku haruka tooku

00:34.980 --> 00:41.590
A gentle voice is calling me

00:34.980 --> 00:41.590
Watashi wo yobu yasashii koe

00:41.610 --> 00:45.190
Let's go look for it

00:41.610 --> 00:45.190
Sagashii ni yukou

00:45.200 --> 00:50.930
Even if we wander aimlessly

00:45.200 --> 00:50.930
Attemonai keredo

00:50.950 --> 00:55.730
The rain comes down

00:50.950 --> 00:55.730
Doushaburi no ame

00:55.750 --> 01:00.440
on a lonely morning

00:55.750 --> 01:00.440
Hitoribocchi no asa

01:00.460 --> 01:04.990
But look, beyond the clouds

01:00.460 --> 01:04.990
Demo hora kumo no mukou

01:05.010 --> 01:09.570
the sunlight is peering at us

01:05.010 --> 01:09.570
Hizashi ga nozoiteruyo

01:09.600 --> 01:11.950
Wipe away your tears

01:09.600 --> 01:11.950
Namida fuite

01:11.970 --> 01:14.870
Look forward

01:11.970 --> 01:14.870
Mae wo muite

01:14.890 --> 01:19.170
and summon all of your strength

01:14.890 --> 01:19.170
Ashimoto chikara komete

01:19.190 --> 01:21.560
Let's walk

01:19.190 --> 01:21.560
Aruite yukou

01:21.570 --> 01:23.920
I'm sure we will make it

01:21.570 --> 01:23.920
Kitto yukeru

01:23.940 --> 01:31.300
The road, the road, continues on...

01:23.940 --> 01:31.300
Michi wa michi wa tsuzuku yo...

01:31.330 --> 01:34.360
forever...

01:31.330 --> 01:34.360
Dokomademo

02:00.560 --> 02:02.750
Cosette, are you still not done yet?!

02:03.110 --> 02:05.130
Ah... Yes, I'm almost done.

02:05.650 --> 02:08.880
There is no time for you to be doing the same thing all day long.

02:09.450 --> 02:11.860
Now you'll clean the tables nice and proper!

02:12.280 --> 02:12.640
Here!

02:16.500 --> 02:18.700
My goodness, you're such a useless runt!

02:20.420 --> 02:22.060
There's no time for you to rest.

02:22.090 --> 02:27.190
After this, you need to polish the great sign which I drew.

02:30.340 --> 02:31.570
Cosette!

02:31.850 --> 02:33.280
Let's play together!

02:33.310 --> 02:33.990
Azelma.

02:33.880 --> 02:34.920
Let's play!

02:34.930 --> 02:36.510
I told you not to say that, Azelma.

02:36.520 --> 02:36.830
What?

02:37.640 --> 02:40.210
Mother said we're not allowed to play with Cosette.

02:40.230 --> 02:45.170
You and I are the Princesses of the Waterloo Inn, but Cosette isn't.

02:46.610 --> 02:48.670
Hey you, get back to work!

02:48.700 --> 02:50.190
Get to work!

02:51.410 --> 02:53.300
Gavroche is crying again.

02:55.240 --> 02:56.060
Shut up!

02:58.460 --> 03:01.230
Geez, for a boy you aren't cute at all.

03:01.880 --> 03:03.560
Be quiet!

03:04.040 --> 03:05.080
Are you still going to cry!?

03:05.550 --> 03:07.070
Mistress!

03:07.090 --> 03:09.530
What? You wanna speak up for him?!

03:09.840 --> 03:12.070
Oh, I know! Cosette...

03:12.890 --> 03:15.830
You can babysit and work at the same time!

03:19.310 --> 03:21.290
What's with your melodramatic fall?

03:21.940 --> 03:24.290
It makes me look like I'm bullying you.

03:24.400 --> 03:26.340
Geez, what an indecent girl you are...

03:26.570 --> 03:28.420
Oh, you're back!

03:28.740 --> 03:32.380
Éponine and Azelma, come here. I have treats for you.

03:32.410 --> 03:33.840
Really?

03:35.330 --> 03:37.350
Don't cry, Gavroche.

03:38.950 --> 03:41.850
"Lullaby, lullaby..."

03:41.870 --> 03:44.190
"Time to sleep..."

03:44.210 --> 03:48.610
"A magical lullaby..."

03:48.630 --> 03:50.940
"Lullaby... If you wipe your tears..."

03:51.680 --> 03:53.320
Thank goodness, he stopped crying.

03:56.140 --> 03:57.280
He's really annoying.

03:57.310 --> 03:59.120
Go take him somewhere else to cry!

04:00.760 --> 04:05.760
Jean Valjean's Secret

04:06.570 --> 04:11.510
"Lullaby... Lullaby... Time to sleep..."

04:12.320 --> 04:17.260
"A magical lullaby..."

04:17.280 --> 04:22.180
"Lullaby... If you wipe your tears..."

04:23.210 --> 04:26.770
"We'll meet in your dreams..."

04:37.140 --> 04:38.530
There, there.

04:50.030 --> 04:54.510
I'm going to find a house where we can live happily as a family.

04:58.120 --> 04:59.140
Mother...

05:07.380 --> 05:10.900
In the factory, men and women are separated.

05:11.800 --> 05:17.530
The factory owner, Monsieur Madeleine, came
up with this to avoid unnecessary trouble.

05:18.090 --> 05:18.820
Zephyrine.

05:18.850 --> 05:19.490
Yes.

05:19.510 --> 05:21.410
Please come over here for a bit.

05:22.770 --> 05:24.540
Good morning, Mademoiselle Mella.

05:25.270 --> 05:28.920
This is Fantine, a new employee. Please look after her.

05:28.940 --> 05:32.060
She said she's a single woman, which is just like you.

05:32.400 --> 05:34.590
Ah, nice to meet you.

05:36.530 --> 05:39.050
Nice to meet you too. I hope we get along well.

05:39.950 --> 05:42.100
Well, we'll start by getting you changed into work clothes.

05:42.120 --> 05:42.810
Come this way.

05:43.450 --> 05:44.430
Okay.

05:49.880 --> 05:51.900
What's with this guy?

05:51.920 --> 05:55.150
Alain, I want to hire you as an errand boy.

05:56.170 --> 05:59.110
It's definitely strange no matter how I think about it.

05:59.140 --> 06:01.280
Is that guy planning on something?

06:02.180 --> 06:04.160
In the first place, I was a thief.

06:04.430 --> 06:07.120
It's just too weird for him to hire me.

06:08.100 --> 06:09.750
I'll decline. It's too dangerous.

06:13.980 --> 06:17.090
But, I really want a job.

06:19.240 --> 06:22.110
Well, it'd be undesirable if he thinks I took the chance to escape.

06:26.000 --> 06:27.180
Good morning, Alain.

06:27.790 --> 06:29.520
Did you like yesterday's treats?

06:30.170 --> 06:31.480
Mayor Madeleine is waiting for you.

06:31.840 --> 06:32.980
Come on, hurry up and go.

06:33.170 --> 06:34.150
Ah, thank you.

06:37.130 --> 06:37.780
Please enter.

06:40.300 --> 06:41.490
Good morning, Alain.

06:41.510 --> 06:43.340
I haven't said I'd take the job...

06:43.350 --> 06:44.090
Good morning.

06:50.100 --> 06:51.290
I'm sorry it's so sudden, but...

06:51.610 --> 06:56.420
Could you take this to Sister Simplice at the hospital in the convent?

06:57.740 --> 07:00.440
I'm telling you, I haven't accepted the job yet!

07:03.160 --> 07:05.970
Please. It's urgent. Do you know the place?

07:07.870 --> 07:10.700
Don't lose it. 1000 francs is enclosed in it.

07:10.790 --> 07:12.650
1000 francs?

07:16.210 --> 07:17.070
Out of my way! Out of my way!

07:24.300 --> 07:26.080
<i>Is he really that foolish?</i>

07:26.680 --> 07:31.040
<i>Entrusting someone he met yesterday, a thief, to carry 1000 francs...</i>

07:31.690 --> 07:35.210
I see. He must have wanted to give me this money!

07:35.360 --> 07:37.630
He wanted me to take it and run away.

07:38.530 --> 07:43.260
With this amount of money, Daniel, Marie
and I can live a carefree life for a while!

07:45.280 --> 07:46.890
Yeah, that has to be it.

07:52.540 --> 07:53.810
Damn.

07:55.040 --> 07:56.230
Dammit!

08:02.380 --> 08:05.410
Hey, Sister Simplice!

08:05.430 --> 08:07.530
Sister Simplice!

08:08.810 --> 08:10.620
Please be quiet in the hospital.

08:11.600 --> 08:14.250
Your collar is crooked. Let me fix it.

08:14.850 --> 08:18.130
Stop that! I have business with Sister Simplice.

08:18.480 --> 08:20.130
I'm Simplice.

08:21.030 --> 08:25.220
You must be Alain. I heard about you from Mayor Madeleine yesterday.

08:25.280 --> 08:29.100
He said a boy who just came to this town runs errands for him.

08:29.370 --> 08:32.560
What's with him, saying unnecessary things about me, dammit!

08:33.580 --> 08:36.100
Please do not say such profane language!

08:37.250 --> 08:39.360
I didn't say anything bad.

08:39.750 --> 08:42.530
You should not lie. Lying is a sin.

08:43.550 --> 08:45.740
Here, I was told to deliver this.

08:46.390 --> 08:48.870
Thank you for your hard work.

08:49.260 --> 08:52.160
Now we can buy new beds and medicine with this.

08:52.810 --> 08:56.420
We can now save many poor people who are
suffering from illness in this hospital.

08:57.020 --> 08:58.250
Poor people?

08:59.190 --> 09:04.090
In order for poor people to obtain free treatment,

09:04.110 --> 09:06.930
Monsieur Madeleine donates money to this hospital.

09:07.740 --> 09:09.140
No way, this must be a lie!

09:09.160 --> 09:10.320
What is a lie?

09:10.700 --> 09:12.640
I would never lie!

09:13.040 --> 09:14.180
Okay.

09:15.960 --> 09:18.190
<i>Just how foolish is he?</i>

09:19.130 --> 09:21.480
Alain, is something wrong?

09:22.710 --> 09:23.610
My...

09:24.920 --> 09:27.170
My mother died of an illness.

09:28.850 --> 09:32.580
She tried to go to a doctor, but she didn't have any money.

09:33.270 --> 09:35.870
Because she didn't have money, the doctor wouldn't treat her!

09:36.440 --> 09:37.120
Alain?

09:41.900 --> 09:46.340
If Mother had been living in this town, she wouldn't have died!

09:46.360 --> 09:47.800
Dammit!

09:59.920 --> 10:03.150
<i>I suppose I can only see what he's planning on doing.</i>

10:18.100 --> 10:19.920
Well, I'm off!

10:20.060 --> 10:22.170
Have a good day, Brother!

10:22.190 --> 10:23.500
Have a good day!

10:23.530 --> 10:24.210
Yeah!

10:25.110 --> 10:26.480
Good morning!

10:31.530 --> 10:32.510
Good morning, Alain.

10:35.830 --> 10:37.680
Good morning, Mayor.

10:39.420 --> 10:40.440
Mayor?

10:41.000 --> 10:41.440
Huh?

10:43.880 --> 10:45.940
Oh, you're here after all.

10:46.260 --> 10:48.440
Mayor. It's me, Alain.

10:49.300 --> 10:51.070
Oh, it's you, Alain.

10:51.470 --> 10:53.070
Why are you in a daze like that?

10:53.300 --> 10:55.160
That's not like you, Mayor.

10:55.560 --> 10:56.240
Yes...

10:57.020 --> 10:59.790
Bishop Myriel has ascended to heaven.

11:01.050 --> 11:04.390
Bishop? A bishop well known enough to be in the newspapers?

11:04.690 --> 11:05.810
Did you know him?

11:07.440 --> 11:08.010
Yes...

11:08.190 --> 11:12.470
A long time ago, I was in his care, in Digne, a city to the south.

11:12.490 --> 11:12.970
I see.

11:14.120 --> 11:17.600
Bishop Myriel was truly a great person.

11:18.830 --> 11:23.440
There isn't a word in this world that is able to describe his greatness.

11:24.000 --> 11:25.400
Aren't you exaggerating?

11:26.000 --> 11:27.360
No, it's really true.

11:27.960 --> 11:31.070
He always treated people kindly, no matter who they were.

11:37.430 --> 11:45.500
Once upon a time, a man called Jean Valjean, who was
released from prison recently, had arrived in Digne.

11:46.070 --> 11:48.000
Jean... Valjean?

12:05.500 --> 12:08.690
So what crime did this guy, Jean Valjean, commit?

12:09.590 --> 12:13.280
He stole a single loaf of bread for his starving nephew and niece.

12:14.510 --> 12:16.070
It was such a minor crime.

12:16.930 --> 12:24.210
But Jean Valjean tried to escape so many times,
so he had to spend 19 years in prison.

12:26.190 --> 12:30.340
Even after he served time for his crimes and was
released from prison, society was cold to him.

12:31.530 --> 12:34.260
Everyone looked down upon him and ostracized him.

12:35.070 --> 12:39.260
He could not even obtain shelter. Even his requests for food were denied.

12:40.700 --> 12:44.350
Nonetheless, Bishop Myriel invited him to his home,

12:44.950 --> 12:48.270
and provided him with food and a soft bed.

12:49.130 --> 12:56.740
However, this Jean Valjean guy stole silverware from the Bishop and ran away.

12:58.680 --> 13:04.330
It's all because it was like being in prison. After he
was released, he was never treated like a person.

13:05.350 --> 13:10.460
In his heart, he had lost something very important.

13:12.940 --> 13:16.930
So what happened to the Bishop? And Jean Valjean?

13:17.530 --> 13:23.060
He... Jean Valjean was immediately caught by
the police and taken to the Bishop's home.

13:24.250 --> 13:27.730
Of course, he thought the Bishop would accuse him of being a thief.

13:29.420 --> 13:31.270
However, the Bishop...

13:34.840 --> 13:39.070
No, I gave that silverware to him.

13:40.760 --> 13:44.870
Jean Valjean, you forgot these.

13:45.940 --> 13:49.330
I did also say that I was giving these silver candlesticks to you.

13:51.940 --> 13:53.380
Here, take them.

13:59.490 --> 14:01.680
You must not forget...

14:02.700 --> 14:07.770
...that you have promised me that you would
use all this silver to turn over a new leaf.

14:14.460 --> 14:15.150
And then?

14:16.130 --> 14:19.200
How's the guy called Jean Valjean doing now?

14:22.310 --> 14:24.160
I don't know what happened afterwards.

14:25.520 --> 14:28.960
<i>I'm sorry, Alain. That was a story about myself.</i>

14:29.650 --> 14:34.880
<i>I am Jean Valjean, but I lack the courage to admit it.</i>

14:35.150 --> 14:38.220
I see. So you don't know what happened afterwards, Mayor.

14:39.160 --> 14:43.970
But I'm sure Jean Valjean is living an honest
life, as if he had turned a new leaf, right?

14:44.620 --> 14:49.310
But somehow, this Bishop sounds a lot like you, Monsieur Madeleine.

14:51.580 --> 14:52.270
Impossible...

14:53.090 --> 14:56.150
I cannot compare to the great man he was.

15:06.770 --> 15:08.970
Cosette, stop wasting time!

15:08.980 --> 15:09.620
Yes.

15:09.640 --> 15:12.040
Cosette, bring me more wine from the back.

15:12.190 --> 15:12.790
Yes.

15:13.060 --> 15:15.460
Cosette, where's my dress?

15:15.480 --> 15:16.420
Where's mine?

15:16.440 --> 15:18.090
They're still not dry.

15:18.110 --> 15:19.800
How come?

15:22.520 --> 15:25.900
Three years later

15:43.090 --> 15:44.740
Oops, I tripped.

15:45.720 --> 15:47.240
How cruel, Éponine.

15:47.520 --> 15:49.260
You're the one who's cruel, Cosette.

15:49.600 --> 15:51.540
You left a bucket here!

15:52.150 --> 15:54.710
Look! My clothes are drenched.

15:54.730 --> 15:55.920
It's drenched!

15:55.940 --> 15:57.310
You did it on purpose...

15:57.730 --> 16:00.260
So, you're being defiant.

16:00.280 --> 16:01.340
Defiant.

16:01.360 --> 16:03.720
I wonder if I should tell Mother.

16:03.740 --> 16:04.800
Tell Mother.

16:12.080 --> 16:13.810
Hurry and clean it up.

16:13.830 --> 16:15.150
Clean it up.

16:16.960 --> 16:19.110
It feels like something dropped on my head.

16:19.590 --> 16:21.110
I can't see.

16:21.340 --> 16:23.110
Ahh! A mouse!

16:25.640 --> 16:27.990
Bullying is bad, right?

16:28.260 --> 16:29.330
Gavroche.

16:30.060 --> 16:32.080
I wanted to throw another one.

16:33.060 --> 16:34.540
I'll help you, Cosette.

16:34.940 --> 16:36.750
Thank you, Gavroche.

16:36.770 --> 16:38.420
I hate mice.

16:38.440 --> 16:40.000
Gavroche must have done that.

16:40.190 --> 16:41.630
He really gets on my nerves.

16:41.820 --> 16:44.090
Éponine, Azelma, I've got a snack for you.

16:44.110 --> 16:45.220
Coming!

16:45.990 --> 16:47.720
Oh, there you are.

16:48.200 --> 16:49.930
I have baked some cakes for you today.

16:50.120 --> 16:52.220
The smell of butter is fragrant, right?

16:52.540 --> 16:56.020
Well then, let's eat them in front of Cosette.

16:56.040 --> 16:57.370
To show them off to her.

16:57.790 --> 17:00.570
Thanks to you it's already clean.

17:00.840 --> 17:02.500
Let me help you even more.

17:02.550 --> 17:03.860
Ah, what a nice smell.

17:03.880 --> 17:04.820
Nice smell.

17:05.550 --> 17:07.530
This looks like a tasty cake.

17:07.550 --> 17:09.090
I'll eat mine here.

17:09.810 --> 17:11.910
They're doing something weird again today.

17:12.140 --> 17:13.750
Don't worry about them.

17:14.810 --> 17:15.930
Let's eat!

17:15.940 --> 17:16.750
Hold on!

17:17.400 --> 17:18.250
Come over here.

17:18.270 --> 17:19.000
What?

17:19.900 --> 17:21.630
I'll put this away.

17:23.150 --> 17:25.170
Come on, put yours in here too.

17:25.450 --> 17:27.010
No, I want to eat it!

17:27.030 --> 17:28.340
I have a good idea.

17:28.740 --> 17:31.760
You see, we'll hide them in here.

17:32.410 --> 17:35.950
And then, we'll tell Mother that Cosette took them from us.

17:37.080 --> 17:40.150
After that, Mother will scold Cosette, right?

17:40.340 --> 17:43.320
Afterwards, we can eat the cakes we hid.

17:43.590 --> 17:44.400
I understand.

17:47.510 --> 17:48.740
Mother!

17:49.260 --> 17:50.160
What's wrong?

17:50.430 --> 17:51.590
Our cakes were taken!

17:51.640 --> 17:52.450
They were taken!

17:52.470 --> 17:54.370
Cosette and Gavroche took them!

17:54.390 --> 17:55.580
Cosette and Gavroche!

17:56.100 --> 17:57.290
The cakes I gave to you?

17:57.310 --> 17:58.290
Yes.

17:59.360 --> 18:00.920
I don't smell any butter.

18:01.690 --> 18:03.880
They were taken before you even had a bite, right?

18:03.900 --> 18:04.420
Yes.

18:04.820 --> 18:07.720
All right, Mother will teach them a lesson!

18:11.080 --> 18:12.050
Cosette!

18:12.080 --> 18:12.570
Yes.

18:12.990 --> 18:14.100
Give them back quickly!

18:15.750 --> 18:21.020
Don't play dumb! You took Éponine and Azelma's cakes, right?

18:21.090 --> 18:22.480
Huh? I don't know.

18:22.500 --> 18:24.980
What?! You think I'll believe that?!

18:25.010 --> 18:26.610
I really don't know.

18:27.010 --> 18:29.610
Well, she already ate them.

18:29.640 --> 18:30.820
Ate them.

18:31.890 --> 18:33.580
There's no scent of butter.

18:34.180 --> 18:36.260
You haven't eaten them. Hurry up and return them!

18:36.310 --> 18:37.160
I don't know anything!

18:37.180 --> 18:37.830
What!?

18:38.850 --> 18:40.790
You're really a nasty child!

18:42.270 --> 18:46.050
You poor children. I'll make you more cakes tomorrow.

18:46.070 --> 18:47.730
Just endure it for today, okay?

18:47.740 --> 18:49.050
Yes, I'll endure it.

18:49.070 --> 18:49.800
I'll endure it.

18:49.820 --> 18:52.930
You're such good children. You're so cute!

18:53.200 --> 18:54.430
It hurts...

18:54.990 --> 18:56.770
Come on, go play in your room now.

18:56.790 --> 18:57.810
Yes!

18:57.830 --> 18:59.640
I'll call you when your meals are ready.

18:59.670 --> 19:00.390
Ouch!

19:05.840 --> 19:07.320
That went well.

19:07.550 --> 19:09.570
Of course! Now, let's eat.

19:10.720 --> 19:12.660
Huh? I'm sure I hid it here.

19:13.510 --> 19:14.450
The tin is gone!

19:22.060 --> 19:23.250
I'm hungry...

19:23.440 --> 19:24.960
Cosette! Cosette!

19:24.980 --> 19:26.250
Huh? Gavroche?

19:26.440 --> 19:27.670
Look! Look!

19:27.900 --> 19:28.800
What is it?

19:31.110 --> 19:31.880
Look.

19:32.990 --> 19:35.800
I found what Éponine and Azelma hid.

19:36.290 --> 19:38.220
Then you should give it back.

19:38.250 --> 19:42.060
But Éponine and Azelma lied to bully you.

19:43.170 --> 19:44.770
Bullying is bad.

19:45.090 --> 19:45.940
Should we eat them?

19:45.960 --> 19:46.770
Yes.

19:46.800 --> 19:48.650
Our snacks are gone!

19:48.670 --> 19:51.400
Cosette and Gavroche did it!

19:51.470 --> 19:55.450
I already heard that. That's why I punished Cosette, remember?

19:55.970 --> 19:58.950
What? What's the matter now?

20:08.440 --> 20:10.170
Ah, that was delicious.

20:10.190 --> 20:11.800
Yeah, it was tasty.

20:13.610 --> 20:15.930
Did your mother go that way?

20:16.160 --> 20:16.720
Yes.

20:17.580 --> 20:19.600
When is your mother coming back?

20:20.000 --> 20:25.560
I don't know, but she said as soon as she finds
a home where we can live happily as a family.

20:25.670 --> 20:29.400
Every morning as I wake up, I would think
to myself, "Will she come back today?"

20:30.010 --> 20:33.820
And as night falls, I would think to myself “Will she come back tomorrow?"

20:34.090 --> 20:36.030
I hope she comes back soon.

20:36.050 --> 20:40.410
Yes, but then I would have to say goodbye to you.

20:41.180 --> 20:43.040
Would you come with us, Gavroche?

20:43.060 --> 20:43.620
Yes.

20:43.640 --> 20:46.140
Gavroche, would you like to be my little brother?

20:46.150 --> 20:47.380
Yeah. Sure.

20:47.400 --> 20:48.460
I'm glad.

20:51.440 --> 20:54.590
Mother, will you come back soon?

20:56.530 --> 20:59.720
Cosette is doing well and has grown.

21:01.620 --> 21:02.740
Cosette...

21:03.290 --> 21:07.620
I know how you're doing from the letters of the kind Thénardier family.

21:08.670 --> 21:12.690
But it pains me to not be able to be close to you.

21:14.470 --> 21:17.240
I want to see you soon, Cosette.

21:20.390 --> 21:22.040
Yes, good work.

21:22.390 --> 21:24.160
This is an excellent report, Alain.

21:24.440 --> 21:27.540
